{"title":"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Faster)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Faster)</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Note\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Note</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Algebra)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Algebra)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Very_Intuitive)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Very Intuitive)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/7/ac75ad8f683f14d3cd16e228ad4a48f4ebd3250e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^{}_{}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Real_number\" title=\"Real number\">real number</a> for which\n</p>\n<div style=\"text-align:center\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/9/d49bf9d61cafb77fc2043857f815732ddef15f57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor r + \\frac{19}{100} \\right\\rfloor + \\left\\lfloor r + \\frac{20}{100} \\right\\rfloor + \\left\\lfloor r + \\frac{21}{100} \\right\\rfloor + \\cdots + \\left\\lfloor r + \\frac{91}{100} \\right\\rfloor = 546.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"496\" height=\"43\" /></div>\n<p>Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/e/afe07abb3d805f683f8de488e7dbaebcf8eede92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor 100r \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"54\" height=\"20\" />. (For real <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f83605c92fe99b2607e4d9c403a0b2f74e32a5a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{}_{}$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/6/06681f5b345750104366c512078960fee8d81b49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor x \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"19\" /> is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Floor_function\" title=\"Floor function\">greatest integer</a> less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f83605c92fe99b2607e4d9c403a0b2f74e32a5a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{}_{}$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />.)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/8/c58a401cd72b99aa50b1ef0edd4a7324d948117c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$91 - 19 + 1 = 73$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"131\" height=\"14\" /> numbers in the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sequence\" title=\"Sequence\">sequence</a>. Since the terms of the sequence can be at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> apart, all of the numbers in the sequence can take one of two possible values. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/c/ebc3a6018497f713b235ac7c613c93b92b64cd5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{546}{73} = 7 R 35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"96\" height=\"37\" />, the values of each of the terms of the sequence must be either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. As the remainder is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7f6c79f2148f0cec592c9517b40ee1b82ef22e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> must take on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7f6c79f2148f0cec592c9517b40ee1b82ef22e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> of the values, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> being the value of the remaining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/d/4ed72de96a54dd0c83e3df216bd6725bb59850f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$73 - 35 = 38$\" width=\"100\" height=\"12\" /> numbers. The 39th number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/d/09d66e28695fa71ef9e32b02322c5f65d721f4c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor r+\\frac{19 + 39 - 1}{100}\\rfloor= \\lfloor r+\\frac{57}{100}\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"240\" height=\"38\" />, which is also the first term of this sequence with a value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/d/d6df799fad60ff11d5c55850b79991db326ad517.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 \\le r + \\frac{57}{100} &lt; 8.01$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"151\" height=\"38\" />. Solving shows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/5/38504df280aba943aaeae9cc329a759fe89f3c31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{743}{100} \\le r &lt; \\frac{744}{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"118\" height=\"38\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/4/b1490c99fccb52ebb85214a64242fe25e2d900a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$743\\le 100r &lt; 744$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"138\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/a/04ad29478fd2b7085d76c5562a2a688464fc6f7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor 100r \\rfloor = \\boxed{743}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"115\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Faster.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Faster)\">Solution 2 (Faster)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Faster)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Recall by Hermite's Identity that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/8/548122d729db491254c082e4dfb5e9a2f8b73c82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor x\\rfloor +\\lfloor x+\\frac{1}{n}\\rfloor +...+\\lfloor x+\\frac{n-1}{n}\\rfloor = \\lfloor nx\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"326\" height=\"37\" /> for positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, and real <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Similar to above, we quickly observe that the last 35 take the value of 8, and remaining first ones take a value of 7. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/4/9347afa1c495ad2b540c4ec1f42de19833636f31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor r\\rfloor \\le ...\\le \\lfloor r+\\frac{18}{100}\\rfloor \\le 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"200\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/a/ada7ba86b51875a27ca77fd9216889ee59d20485.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor r+1\\rfloor \\ge ...\\ge \\lfloor r+\\frac{92}{100}\\rfloor \\ge 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"233\" height=\"38\" />. We can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/c/04c0c6f26ab7088b6131c7c4b1a9ce911d10aadd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor r\\rfloor +1=\\lfloor r+1\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"19\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/7/457542ffc4f4a0decfec8869d77fce8582690bfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor r\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"22\" height=\"19\" /> is at most 7, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/0/e80e1c38bbf5936891b4b3a9bce2848b03422d90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor r+1\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"53\" height=\"19\" /> is at least 8, we can clearly see their values are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. \nSo,  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/8/e1827e4358f31791219f14a1fa63477a7c25de7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor r\\rfloor = ... = \\lfloor r+\\frac{18}{100}\\rfloor = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"200\" height=\"38\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/3/3a3a2852da12028bcf4d3e87ad2342434fdfb7fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor r+\\frac{92}{100}\\rfloor = ...= \\lfloor r+1\\rfloor = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"231\" height=\"38\" />. Since there are 19 terms in the former equation and 8 terms in the latter, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/7/bd7c0d16be1f74a7914888b6729a260f92e1c227.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor nx\\rfloor = 546+19\\cdot 7+8\\cdot 8=\\boxed{743}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"268\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>~ minor edit by arjunkhokhar\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Note\">Note</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Note\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>In the contest, you would just observe this mentally, and then calculate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10fcf738a791bb48baa23d0c643992cdee42974d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$546+19\\cdot 7+8\\cdot 8= 743$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"197\" height=\"15\" />, hence the speed at which one can carry out this solution.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Algebra.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Algebra)\">Solution 3 (Algebra)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Algebra)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice how all terms in this series is in the form \\( \\lfloor r + \\frac{k}{100} \\rfloor \\), where \\( 19 \\le k \\le 91 \\). This then implies that there are a total of 73 terms in this series.\n</p><p>If every term is the same, i.e., \\( 73 \\lfloor r + \\frac{19}{100} \\rfloor = 546 \\), then \\( \\lfloor r + \\frac{19}{100} \\rfloor = \\frac{546}{7} \\approx 7 \\). However, because this isn't exactly 7, this implies that the values in the series are mixed between 7 and 8, so we need to do a bit more work to find out the value of \\( k \\) such that \\( \\lfloor r + \\frac{k}{100} \\rfloor = 7 \\) and \\( \\lfloor r + \\frac{k+1}{100} \\rfloor = 8 \\).\n</p><p>We see that if we have a values that return 7 and b values that return 8, then \\( a+b=73 \\).\n</p><p>Additionally, because the total sum of all values is 546, we have \\( 7a + 8b = 546 \\).\n</p><p>Solving the system returns \\( b=35 \\), so 35 terms return 8 and the others return 7.\n</p><p>Then, it is notable that the last 35 terms of the series will return 8 (as they are the ones that maximize the value of r), and of course, we have \\( k+1=91-35+1 =57 \\). So \\( k = 56 \\).\n</p><p>Therefore, the point of change occurs in the step from \\( \\lfloor r + \\frac{56}{100} \\rfloor \\) to \\( \\lfloor r + \\frac{57}{100} \\rfloor \\).\n</p><p>We now use the definition of \\( \\lfloor r + \\frac{57}{100} \\rfloor = 8 \\), because if \\( \\lfloor r + \\frac{56}{100} \\rfloor = 7 \\), that would imply that \\( \\{r\\} = \\frac{100-57}{100} = \\frac{43}{100} \\) (as \\( \\lfloor \\frac{56+43}{100} \\rfloor = 0 \\) and \\( \\lfloor \\frac{57+43}{100} \\rfloor = 1 \\))\n</p><p>Then, through the definition of \\( \\{r\\} \\), we see that \\( r - \\lfloor r \\rfloor = \\{r\\} \\), and because \\( \\lfloor r \\rfloor = 7 \\) and \\( \\{r\\} = \\frac{43}{100} \\), we get \\( r = \\frac{743}{100} = 7.43 \\).\n</p><p>\\( \\lfloor 100r \\rfloor = \\lfloor 100 \\cdot 7.43 \\rfloor = \\lfloor 743 \\rfloor = \\) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/1/141c57f64cb7d2c8fcc5c1b5ca1abe140951e558.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{743}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Very_Intuitive.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Very_Intuitive)\">Solution 4 (Very Intuitive)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Very Intuitive)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/2/e322700e9ce638364b3fff799a5ecba43b5d4be3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = \\lfloor r \\rfloor \\text{, for some integer } k \\in \\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"237\" height=\"20\" />.\nPlugging in into the expression simplifies into,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/4/db41a82dc6ae717f9c3d78252d65938e1dc3d42d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[73k = 546 \\Rightarrow k = \\frac{546}{73} = 7.479...\\]\" width=\"251\" height=\"38\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> must be an integer, this can't be a solution. Instead, in order for it to be a solution, the numerator must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/b/b5b03f8ead3b3da0bd2cbc1a41d8f01630e638f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$73$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Notice that the closest multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/b/b5b03f8ead3b3da0bd2cbc1a41d8f01630e638f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$73$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/a/3aa6c57b59a2ac2c8983b6b771f69d9a8d3d793e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$546$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/6/06681161db752e0642652340b0832dcdaecefde0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$511$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/2/c425450b4f85813f478814194b31105c05052cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$546 - 511 = 35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"15\" />. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> will have an integer solution if we can achieve the expression <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/f/2ff87a637bef77cdf0fe13a672de3e8fd66bb646.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$73k + 35 = 546$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"122\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>The last term of the sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/1/68148a5859fa254a988709dcda534da1e0067c7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor r + \\frac{91}{100} \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"75\" height=\"38\" /> , and in order for that floor function to equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/8/e18453e31b8b9f4f7722777b72a0eff030a17d1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> must be in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/6/e96376faf301bb21d1f93b1b8930815615f24c49.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r = k + 0.09 + 0.01x \\text{, for some real number } x \\in \\mathbb{R}, 0 \\le x &lt; 1\\]\" width=\"461\" height=\"16\" />\nThis needs to go on until the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7f6c79f2148f0cec592c9517b40ee1b82ef22e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />th last term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/8/6a8412a5c510f7b52aacb51b2b8ab52a328a5866.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\text{from } \\left\\lfloor r + \\frac{57}{100} \\right\\rfloor \\text{ to } \\left\\lfloor r + \\frac{91}{100} \\right\\rfloor\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"268\" height=\"45\" /> in order to achieve <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/f/2ff87a637bef77cdf0fe13a672de3e8fd66bb646.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$73k + 35 = 546$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"122\" height=\"16\" />. For this to happen, the last 35 terms must each equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/8/e18453e31b8b9f4f7722777b72a0eff030a17d1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" />, hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> must satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/d/49d766d38e52a073a09270843f25c106df8a9756.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = k + 0.43 + 0.01x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"164\" height=\"16\" />.\nHence, we achieve,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/1/4d120f224190fc545a75630170b53b33c7f7f800.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[73k + 35 = 546\\]\" width=\"118\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/2/5d2adeaa02920b3e601b65f61fd67e2513c09ee8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[73k = 511 \\Rightarrow k = 7\\]\" width=\"150\" height=\"13\" />\nWhich means,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/8/68854a9fd31326118d61802937cc15d60b093a99.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r = k + 0.43 + 0.01x \\Rightarrow r = 7.43 + 0.01x\\]\" width=\"319\" height=\"14\" />\nHence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/0/af047eb3aa9394a8a45d091e9ad99a7d919d5f2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor 100r \\rfloor = \\lfloor 743 + x \\rfloor = \\boxed{743}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"217\" height=\"25\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME\" title=\"1991 AIME\">1991 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1991 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1991\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017063407\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.043 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.064 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 394/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1766/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 88/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 11873/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.563      1 -total\n 60.11%    7.551      1 Template:AIME_box\n 38.21%    4.800      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2905:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017063407 and revision id 288541. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}